-- statement:
--   The theorem states that, for a Coxeter matrix M on a finite linearly ordered generating set S, with Artin(M) the Artin group presented by the braid relations determined by M (alternating words of length M(s,t) in s and t are equal), every subset E of Artin(M) lies in a unique smallest parabolic subgroup. Here a subgroup P is parabolic if it is a conjugate g·Artin_parabolic(T)·g⁻¹ of the standard subgroup generated by the images of the generators in some subset T of S, for some g in Artin(M), with no spherical-type restriction. Precisely, there exists exactly one subgroup P of Artin(M) that is parabolic, contains E, and is contained in every parabolic subgroup Q that contains E. The statement holds unconditionally, for arbitrary M and arbitrary E, and its proof is admitted in the source rather than established.
